User-facing managed emulators default to the Google Play image (google_apis_playstore) instead of google_apis. Decided with the user: end users need the Play Store + real Google sign-in; the cost is no 'adb root' (production 'user' build), which is fine because the control path (input tap / screencap / uiautomator) needs no root — verified live (adb root => 'cannot run as root in production builds'). Encoded as android::sdk::DEFAULT_SYSTEM_IMAGE (single source of truth) + DEFAULT_DEVICE_PROFILE; doctor hints reference it; ADR-024 documents the rationale. Our own dev AVD (xpressclaw_test) stays on google_apis for rootability; the user-facing one is xpressclaw_play.
